WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.800
What up y'all? This week we callin it with
No Country for Old Men by Cormac McCarthy.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.470
Down in the SouthWest side of Texas, country 
boy Llewelyn Moss rollin strapped through

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:32.840
the dessert huntin antelope when- "Oh damn.
Da hell happened ova' here?" Bodies EVERYWHERE.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.690
And from the look of the gats deez boys was 
packin, this musta been some kinda drug deal

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:43.770
gone HELLA wrong. One dude still breathin
and all like "..say, can you hook a brutha

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:48.780
up with some water?" But Moss just like " Psh.
b*tch I don't know you!" After scopin out

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:54.090
da area some mo, he finds the last brutha
standing and a leather case full of BIG FACES.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:01:00.050
I'm talkin 2.4 MILLION DOLLAS. Oooh baby!

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:05.939
Moss head back home to count his fat stacks, but
start feelin like a real dick leavin that

00:01:05.939 --> 00:01:10.310
Mexican dude hangin. So he head back to the
spot with a jug of water and gets outta his

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:16.090
car, which is about the STUPIDEST damn thing
he coulda done. It aint long before he realize

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:21.770
he ain't out in da boonies by himself, there's
some creep lurkin round his whip. "Oh. F**k."

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:26.630
Moss try to bail but dem pushers chase his
ass through the desert. Eventually, he manage

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:31.740
to shake them off, and calls up his lady Carla
Jean and tell her she gotta bust ass over

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.720
to her mama's house til things cool off a bit.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:40.290
When wind of this mess comes to old law man
Ed Tom Bell, he decide he gonna make sho dat

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:45.649
Moss and Carla Jean make it out alive. Specially
since he did some bunk sh*t back in WW2, and

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:51.049
wanna do some good to make up fo it. But
sh*t gets real whack when a hitman named Anton

00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:57.509
Chigur hit da streets to hunt down dat cash.
This is one cat you DON'T f**k with. Chigur

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:03.000
packin a silenced shotgun and an air-powered
stun gun that not only can blow a hole in

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.869
a brutha's head, but can rip the locks off
doors like it ain't nuthin.

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:12.090
Also hot on the trail of dem Benjamins is
Carson Wells, anotha  hit man, who got beef

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:17.220
with Chigur. Chigur catch up with
Moss across the border, and they start bustin

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:22.500
caps in eachotha til both of em walk away
with gnarly wounds. Chigur patch himself up

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:28.390
in a hotel like a real hardass while Moss
rest up in a hospital. Wells drop in on Moss

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:33.900
and be like "say dawg, you have no idea who
you dealin with. Chigurh ain't gonna stop

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:39.860
lookin for you even if he gets the money back.
He still gon find you and put yo ass six feet

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.440
deep. But I'll take care of him for you
if you gimme dat cheddar."

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:48.620
Wells leaves, and Moss marinate on it fo
a while, but it's too late. Chigur corners

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:54.230
Wells and mercs his ass right as Moss callin
Wells to seal the deal. Chigur pick up da

00:02:54.230 --> 00:03:00.860
phone and tell Moss dat he better  cough up
da cash or he gonna kill Carla Jean. Damn,

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.920
son. Sh*t just got real.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:07.379
Since Carla Jean start to bug out, she call
up Sherriff Ed to tell him where Moss is gonna

00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:12.230
lay low. Guess who traced the call? Das right.
Crazy-ass Chigur.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:18.709
So when Ed Tom's crusty ass swang over to
the motel, he finds Moss lyin in chalk. Apparently,

00:03:18.709 --> 00:03:24.120
he got smoked by a gang of drug pushers also
searchin fo the money. Good lookin out

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:30.239
ED! Later, Chigur roll up on dat motel room
and find the money stashed in the vent and

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:31.890
hand it over to the big dawg.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:37.159
Since Chigur's a man of his word, he stop
by to put a bullet in Carla Jean's dome. She

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:43.180
beg him to just chill, so he flips a coin
to decide her life. (gunshot) She dead. On

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:49.239
his way outta da crib BAM, boy gets TOOKEN
out by a car. He still alive, tho. After bribing

00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:53.459
two kids to keep they mouths shut, Chigur
limps off in to the sunset.

00:03:53.459 --> 00:03:58.830
After tryin to bring the law down on Chigur's
ass fo a while, Old ass Ed just says "f**k

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:05.180
it," retires, and starts talkin bout two trippy
dreams he had after his dad died: In one,

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:10.330
he gotta borrow some ends from his dad, but
just loses em. In da otha, brutha on a horse

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.500
watching his daddy ahead of him holding a
blazin horn,

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:17.769
knowin he would light a fire dat would keep
on blazin in the darkness.

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:19.080
 

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.870
From da first pages of da book, Sherriff Ed
Tom Bell lay it on thick. The world has left

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:31.889
his ass in the dust. See back in his daddy's
day, the hardest hoods on the block would

00:04:31.889 --> 00:04:35.240
jus boost cattle, and chasin em down wasn't
no thang. But these days, da face of evil

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:40.910
got a way meaner mug on it- and Ed Tom and
his boys ain't never seen nothin like it.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:46.009
Deez killas ain't got no code. They'll merc
anybody without even trippin. Like he say

00:04:46.009 --> 00:04:52.660
on page 196, "the world is goin to hell in
a handbasket." This truly is no country for

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:53.590
old men.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:58.600
And speakin of the title, it actually come
from an old school poem by my main man WB

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:03.530
Yeats called "Sailing to Byzantium." In da
poem, the narrator lay down some sick rhymes

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:08.360
bout how how bad it sucks to get old. So he
pack up his nuts and head to Byzantium where

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:14.030
word is some sages gonna appear in fire and
take him outside of time, kinda like da dream

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:16.150
Ed Tom's dream at the end of the book. He
could see his pops "carryin fire in a horn

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:16.289
the way people used to do... in the dream
I knew that he was going on ahead and that

00:05:16.289 --> 00:05:21.080
he was fixin to make a fire somwehere out
there in all that dark.... Whenever I got

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:26.570
world" thing is da same kinda bullshit Ed
Tom Bell and a buncha otha bruthas goin through

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:32.590
in the novel. They da old men constantly sweatin
da coming of the "new man," and da kinda person

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:37.850
you gotta become to stop such stone cold killers.
Like Ed Tom say-

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:42.009
"Somewhere out there is a true and living
prophet of destruction and I dont want to

00:05:42.009 --> 00:05:46.270
confront him. I know he's real. I have seen
his work. I walked in front of those eyes

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:51.560
once. I wont do it again. I wont push my chips
forward and stand up and go out to meet him.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:56.530
It aint just bein older. I wish that it was.
I cant say that it's even what you are willin

00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:00.780
to do. I think it is more like what you are
willin to become. And I think a man would

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.630
have to put his soul at hazard." (4)

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:08.020
Ain't nobody representin this "new man" better
than Anton Chigur- the baddest muthaf**ka

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:13.530
EVER. Yeah, he cold blooded as hell, but there's
more to it than that. Accordin to Wells,

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:19.050
"You could even say he has principles. Principles
that transcend money or drugs or anything

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:19.669
like that." (153)

00:06:19.669 --> 00:06:25.020
Chigur don't look at life like most people
and always be philosophizin like a muthaf**ka,

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:29.970
"I got here the same way the coin did, for
things at a common destination there is a

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:35.910
common path. Not always easy to see. But there, every
moment in your life is a turning and every

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:41.539
one a choosing. Somewhere you made a choice.
All followed to this. The accounting is scrupulous.

00:06:41.539 --> 00:06:44.710
The shape is drawn. No line can be erased."
(258-59)

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:50.039
To Chigur, ain't nobody can really change
the world or da shit that happens. In his

00:06:50.039 --> 00:06:54.480
eyes, asking questions like "Why couldn't
things be different?" just don't make no sense.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:07:00.830
Things are they way they are and we just passively
participating in this cosmic clusterf**k-

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:06.000
like little puzzle pieces that all randomly
come together to create the here and then.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.630
Aight so Ed Tom is the good guy, tryna keep
it old school morality, and Chigur is the

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:16.849
bad guy cuz da new man don't give a shit
bout nuthin, right? Well not exactly. There

00:07:16.849 --> 00:07:22.250
are some pretty interesting similarities between
Ed Tom And Chigur. They both always bustin

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:27.199
other people's balls bout not speakin clearly
enough and both like to go on and on about

00:07:27.199 --> 00:07:28.220
truth and principle.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:33.240
Now here's where shit gets cray: Ed Tom Bell
straight up say "I'm not the man of an older

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:39.430
time they say I am." Huh? Turns out ol Ed
turned his back on his boys back in WW2 and

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:44.610
left them out to die, even though that goes
against his code. Chigur on the other hand,

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:49.840
always talkin bout how he's a man of his word,
like when he's havin one last talk with Carla

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:50.210
Jean,

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:55.810
"You've got no cause to hurt me, she said.
/ I know. But I gave my word…my word is

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:58.379
not dead. Nothing can change that. (256)

00:07:58.379 --> 00:08:00.310
So NOW who's the man with no code?

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:05.690
Also, when a book slangin religious imagery,
they usually doin it to make da good guy look

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:11.610
dat much mo righteous. But in No Country,
it's CHIGUR who all holy like. For real. For

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:16.270
real, when he ghost dat dude on the highway,
da book say "he places his hand on the man's

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:22.379
head like a faith healer." Hm. Later, dude
actually compares himself to actin like God.

00:08:22.379 --> 00:08:29.229
"Even a nonbeliever might find it useful to
model himself after God. Very useful, in fact."

00:08:29.229 --> 00:08:29.970
(256)

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:36.180
And just think abut his piece, one of Chigurh's
favorite ways to ice somebody is with a stungun

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:41.769
used to knock cattle da f**k out. Maybe it's
cuz to someone like Chigurh, who da novel paints

00:08:41.769 --> 00:08:55.129
as mo divine than human, errybody else just
mooin sacks of flesh. God Damn.

